.TH iron-vault-rm 1  "Iron Vault" "Iron Vault Manual"
.SH NAME
iron\-vault\-rm \- Remove the credential NAME after you type the approval passphrase. It refuses while a route of the active config uses the name: approve a config without those routes first
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBiron\-vault rm\fR [\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove the credential NAME after you type the approval passphrase. It refuses while a route of the active config uses the name: approve a config without those routes first
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Use the admin socket at PATH instead of this installation\*(Aqs, for example one forwarded over SSH. Every client command takes it; `serve` refuses it, because the service always binds its own installation\*(Aqs socket
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
The credential name to remove
